course: dictionary
lesson: 394
title: The apostrophe
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An apostrophe is a small mark that looks like a tiny raised comma: '. It has two main jobs. The first is to show that letters are missing from a short word: «don't» is a squeezed form of «do not», and the apostrophe sits where the o has gone.
explain: The second job is to show that something belongs to someone: «Sam's bag» means the bag that belongs to Sam. Ask yourself: is a letter missing, or is something owned? That tells you which job the apostrophe is doing.
explain: Poets sometimes use the word in a different, more formal way. In a poem, a speaker may talk straight to someone who is not there, or to a thing, like «O Moon!». You will meet this mostly when you read poems.
fact: An apostrophe is a punctuation mark: '.
fact: «Don't» means «do not», and the apostrophe shows the missing letter o.
fact: «Sam's bag» shows that the bag belongs to Sam.
fact: «The dog's bone» means one dog; «the dogs' bones» means more than one dog.
fact: «Its» belongs to it and has no apostrophe; «it's» means «it is» or «it has».
exercise: In «I can't come today», what does the apostrophe show? | *Missing letters, because «can't» squeezes «can not» together | A question is being asked | Something belonging to someone | More than one thing
exercise: Which phrase shows that the bag belongs to Sam? | Sam bag | Sams bag | *Sam's bag
exercise: Which word means «it is»? | its | hits | *it's | is
test: Which is correct for more than one dog's bone? | *the dogs' bones | the dogs bones | the dog's bones | the dogs's bones
test: Which shows a letter is missing? | *could've, for could have | Sam's bag | the girls' coats | Its tail is long
exam: Which sentence is correct? | Its' a sunny day | Apple's for sale today | The teacher's were happy | *The girls' coats are on the hook
